+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:149
+msgid ""
+"Request JSON uses the existing 10 MiB options ceiling and separate 128 MiB "
+"record-construction account. Registry/context compilation, source decoding, "
+"structural expansion, output/writer construction, host input/ABI transfer "
+"and result-handle storage retain their separate authorities. The output byte "
+"ceiling is enforced before each governed append, including escaping and "
+"UTF-8; the output allocation ceiling covers newly owned text and traversal "
+"storage. No unbounded intermediate JSON string is constructed. These limits "
+"do not claim total operation-memory accounting. Native diagnostics and "
+"storage causes are retained."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:158
+msgid ""
+"Rust callers use `purrdf_validate::document_expansion::expand(source, "
+"request_json)`. `request(request_json)` compiles a reusable request, and "
+"`expand_decoded(source, &request)` avoids decoding it again. The CLI decodes "
+"and compiles the request before acquiring source bytes; `-` selects stdin/"
+"stdout, and request and source cannot share stdin:"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:168
+msgid ""
+"C callers use `purrdf_document_expand(source, source_len, request_json, "
+"request_len, out_buffer, out_error)`. Both pointer/length inputs are "
+"required. Valid output slots are cleared before work, aliased output/error "
+"slots are refused, and failures publish no buffer. Read successful bytes "
+"with `purrdf_buffer_data`, then call `purrdf_buffer_free`; the output lives "
+"independently of source/request storage. Errors use the existing diagnostic "
+"and native-cause accessors and `purrdf_error_free` lifetime."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:176
+msgid ""
+"Python exposes `purrdf.expand_document(source: bytes, *, request_json: "
+"bytes) -> str`. Immutable input owners remain borrowed while native work "
+"runs outside the GIL. JavaScript exposes `expandDocument(source: Uint8Array, "
+"requestJson: Uint8Array): string`. Its captured non-shared buffers receive "
+"admitted native copies; request admission and compilation precede source "
+"capture. Detached/shared buffers refuse. Both interfaces return JSON text "
+"and retain existing diagnostic/cause error fields. The JavaScript native "
+"cause retains its existing `YamlSourceCause` owner and `free()` lifetime."
+msgstr ""
