+"buffer/error slots as `purrdf_document_expand`, with the same one-buffer "
+"ownership and free functions. Python functions accept `source: bytes` and "
+"keyword-only `request_json: bytes`, returning `str` while retaining the "
+"borrowed-input lifetime. JavaScript functions accept two `Uint8Array` "
+"arguments and return JSON text; admitted capture, retained native causes and "
+"their `free()` lifetime are unchanged."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:273
+msgid ""
+"Native orchestration can use `expand_jsonld_document_with_context` or "
+"`expand_yamlld_document_with_context` to retain "
+"`JsonLdExpandedDocument::document_base` alongside the expanded `value`. "
+"`CompiledJsonLdContext::compile_with_bases` reuses the existing compiler "
+"with independent retrieval and initial semantic bases. `flatten_expanded` "
+"exposes the existing normative node-map construction; the existing value-"
+"only expansion and flattening entry points retain their behavior."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:280
+msgid "Native document compaction"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:282
+msgid ""
+"`compact_expanded_with_context` compacts lexical JSON values before RDF "
+"lowering. `compact_jsonld_with_context` and `compact_yamlld_with_context` "
+"first expand input bytes with a compiled input context, then compact with a "
+"distinct compiled output context. Both return an owned lexical JSON value; "
+"YAML input keeps its existing selection options and expansion limits. Opaque "
+"JSON and native numeric lexemes remain document values rather than taking an "
+"RDF round trip."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:289
+msgid ""
+"Pass `JsonLdCompactionPolicy` with `compact_arrays` and "
+"`compact_to_relative`; both default to `true`. Relative selection affects "
+"document-position IRIs under the compiled base without altering the retained "
+"output context. The compact operation attaches a non-null context, turns an "
+"empty root array into an object, and envelopes other remaining arrays with "
+"the context's `@graph` alias."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:295
+msgid ""
+"Flattening with an output context composes through that same root operation:"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:316
+msgid ""
+"`JsonLdCompactionLimits::max_allocation_bytes` defaults to 32 GiB. It admits "
+"newly owned document output, retained context copies, walk frames and "
+"compactor scratch before construction. Borrowed input and initial compiled "
+"contexts are not charged again. Context compilation, scoped context state "
+"and native IRI/inverse-selection scratch retain their separate semantic "
+"limits; those are per compilation, not an aggregate retained-byte bound. "
+"This is a document-construction account, not a cap on total operation "
+"memory. Expansion and flattening keep their own accounts."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:324
+msgid ""
+"Configured RDF writers project their prepared RDF nodes into this same "
+"compactor, retaining streamed envelopes and one-node residency. Lists, "
+"reifiers, reverse relocation and lossless graph ownership remain RDF "
+"preparation. A selected custom graph index consumes the actual mapping "
+"property's first compacted key and retains residual values, graph "
+"identifiers and other metadata. It does not substitute semantic `@index` "
+"metadata for that property."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:331
+msgid ""
+"The shared value-compaction rules can emit plain strings for untyped "
+"literals even under prefix-only property spellings. Ordinary type/index maps "
+"now use the native document algorithm as well. Multiple lists retain "
+"explicit list objects when one list container would combine their "
+"identities. If an immutable context shadows every lossless spelling, "
+"compaction returns an actionable error. These configured outputs can be more "
+"compact than earlier carrier output. The untyped no-base, no-options "
+"expanded byte baseline is retained. Node types use IRI strings in both JSON-"
+"LD and YAML-LD. RDF JSON literals keep typed lexical forms whenever raw JSON "
+"coercion would change their spelling, collection shape or annotation "
+"identity."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:342
+msgid "Document framing across hosts"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:344
+msgid ""
+"Framing accepts original source bytes, original frame bytes and separate "
+"version-one request JSON. It calls the native two-document byte adapter "
+"directly; that adapter owns both expansions, the node map, framing, "
+"compaction and root finishing. No RDF dataset or additional expansion is "
+"introduced."
+msgstr ""
