+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:427
+msgid ""
+"Python exposes `frame_document(source: bytes, frame: bytes, *, request_json: "
+"bytes) -> str`; all immutable owners remain borrowed while native work runs "
+"outside the GIL. JavaScript exposes `frameDocument(source: Uint8Array, "
+"frame: Uint8Array, requestJson: Uint8Array): string`. Request capture and "
+"compilation precede separately admitted source/frame captures. Returned JSON "
+"text and retained native-cause ownership, including `free()`, follow the "
+"other document operations."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:434
+msgid "Native document framing"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:436
+msgid ""
+"`native_codecs::jsonld::frame_value_with_context` frames a lexical JSON "
+"document; `frame_jsonld_with_context` and `frame_yamlld_with_context` decode "
+"input and frame bytes before calling the same operation. YAML uses the "
+"existing first/all-document selection in `YamlLdOptions`. The algorithm "
+"targets [JSON-LD 1.1 Framing, Recommendation of 16 July 2020, sections 4–5.3]"
+"(https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/REC-json-ld11-framing-20200716/). It expands "
+"through the structural walker, retains the original graph-local node map, "
+"frames iteratively, and uses the shared compactor. It does not lower through "
+"RDF or reconstruct the map from flattened output."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:445
+msgid ""
+"The context arguments have separate roles. `input_context` interprets the "
+"input. `frame_context` supplies initial pattern terms and the offline "
+"registry; `frame_retrieval_base` resolves frame references and local/"
+"registered contexts. The frame's own `@context` is compiled independently "
+"for output using that retrieval base. A missing frame context emits an empty "
+"context; explicit null emits null. Initial pattern terms are not implicitly "
+"emitted. Registry lookup remains offline. `JsonLdFramingBase::Input`, `None` "
+"and `Iri` select the initial output compaction base: the expanded input "
+"document base, no base, or an explicit absolute IRI. The frame's own output "
+"context is then processed over that initial base, with its separate "
+"retrieval URL for context lookup. Its explicit `@base`, including null, "
+"takes effect. Output selection does not change the emitted context document "
+"or the initial pattern context's active meaning."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:458
+msgid ""
+"`JsonLdFramingPolicy` defaults to `JsonLdEmbed::Once`, with `explicit`, "
+"`require_all`, `omit_default` and `frame_default` false, and `omit_graph` "
+"true. Frame-local `@embed`, `@explicit`, `@requireAll` and `@omitDefault` "
+"override the operation defaults for that frame. Implicit child frames "
+"inherit the effective local flags; explicit child frames begin with "
+"operation defaults before applying their own controls. Embedding admits "
+"exactly `@once`, `@always` and `@never`; true aliases `@once`, false aliases "
+"`@never`. Ancestor cycles retain references under every policy. Traversal "
+"follows lexical subject and property order. The nested "
+"`JsonLdCompactionPolicy` retains both defaults, `compact_arrays: true` and "
+"`compact_to_relative: true`, and keyword aliases select output spellings. "
+"Root finishing follows section 5.1's concrete sequence: ordinary compaction "
+"first, then a forced graph envelope only when `omit_graph` is false. "
+"Consequently, `compact_arrays: false` retains a root array and its ordinary "
+"graph envelope even for one result with `omit_graph: true`. The REC's "
+"general omitGraph prose describes multiple-node envelopes but does not "
+"supply an additional true-case unwrapping step after compaction."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:475
+msgid ""
+"Framing uses the merged graph by default. `frame_default: true`, or a top-"
+"level frame property expanding to `@graph`, selects the default graph; a "
+"graph subframe enters the corresponding named graph. The REC API initializes "
+"its graph name to false and immediately tests for `@merged`. This "
+"implementation reads that internal inconsistency using sections 4.1 and 5.3, "
+"which specify the merged/default choice."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:481
+msgid ""
+"`JsonLdFramingLimits` preserves separate `expansion`, `node_map` and "
+"`compaction` construction accounts. Its new framing allowance defaults to 32 "
+"GiB and admits new graph views, output, work frames, typed default markers "
+"and scratch before allocation. Inputs and compiled contexts are borrowed. "
+"Context compilation, scope state and resolver scratch retain their separate "
+"authority; there is no aggregate operation-memory claim. `max_work` defaults "
+"to 2^30 deterministic units, charging subject/property scans, matching, "
+"inherited subframes, recursive matching and embedding. Frame expansion and "
+"context compilation precede that counter. `max_emitted_nodes` defaults to "
+"2^24 subject occurrences, including identifier-only references. Limits "
+"refuse before governed work and return no partial document. Native storage "
+"diagnostics retain their original cause."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/concepts/jsonld.md:493
+msgid ""
+"Native RDF 1.2 triple terms and attached/detached annotations are atomic "
+"framing values. Ordinary property wildcards and exclusions can retain or "
+"exclude them; patterns inspecting `@triple`, its component controls, or "
+"`@annotation` internals are explicitly refused. Identifier references inside "
+"native terms count when pruning singly occurring blank-node identifiers, but "
+"cleanup never changes the atomic values. Opaque `@json` payloads are copied "
+"and compared as whole values, never interpreted or rewritten as JSON-LD. "
+"Private preservation markers occupy separate typed state; ordinary user "
+"strings, including `@null`, and real JSON null cannot become cleanup "
+"instructions."
+msgstr ""
+
