+msgid ""
+"Every validation entry point is fallible. `ValidationError::ShapeMap` "
+"retains shape-map admission errors, `Regex` retains the native XPath cause, "
+"and `MatcherWork { attempted, maximum }` means assignment search could not "
+"finish. No verdict or partial result map is returned on refusal, including "
+"under `NOT`, `AND` or `OR`."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/validation/shex.md:108
+msgid ""
+"Rust callers select `ValidationOptions::matcher_limits` with "
+"`MatcherLimits::new(maximum_states)`. Python uses `matcher_maximum_states=`; "
+"the CLI uses `--matcher-maximum-states COUNT`. The default admits 200,000 "
+"states per ambiguous neighbourhood. Each entered assignment prefix costs one "
+"state, including its terminal cardinality check; rollback and resuming a "
+"candidate cost nothing. Unique predicate assignments require no search "
+"allowance. Zero refuses the first ambiguous state. A refusal reports the "
+"attempted state as maximum plus one, represented exactly even at the largest "
+"`u64` limit. A later validation may admit more work; refused operations are "
+"never memoized as conformance results. Python raises `ValueError` with "
+"message identity `shex-matcher-work` and unsigned `attempted` and `maximum` "
+"presentation parameters."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/validation/shex.md:120
+msgid ""
+"`ValidationOptions` is non-exhaustive. Construct it with `Default` and "
+"select policy with `with_matcher_limits`, `with_external_resolver`, "
+"`with_sem_acts` or `with_extern_start_acts`; its existing fields can also be "
+"updated individually. For example, "
+"`ValidationOptions::default().with_matcher_limits(MatcherLimits::new(1_000_000))` "
+"admits a larger assignment search without selecting a different pattern law."
+msgstr ""
+
